<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#SocietyTitle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named office or titled position within an initiatory society, distinct from grade level. Titles may be elected, inherited, purchased, or conferred. Examples: Iyamba (Abakuá), Isue (Abakuá), Ekueñón (Abakuá), Apetebi Ogboni, Olori Egungun. Each title carries specific ritual functions, insignia, and governance authority. Title names are community-restricted; the ritual functions attached to them are initiated-only."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#lodgeName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#SocietyLodge> .
