<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#society-abakua> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Abakuá mutual aid and initiatory society founded in Cuba in 1836, derived from Ékpè/Ngbe through enslaved Efik and Efut practitioners in Havana and Matanzas. Organized into potencias (lodges), each with a specific founding charter and ranked titleholders. Known in Cuban public life through the íremes (diablito masquerades) which appear at funerals and public ceremonies. Male-only by tradition (juramento)."@en .
