<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#society-gelede> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A masquerade society of the Yorùbá, Nago, and Fon peoples honoring the power of women, especially elder women, ancestresses, and the mothers (àwọn ìyá wa). Gelede festivals feature carved wooden masks worn by male dancers who embody female spiritual authority. UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage. Active in Nigeria, Benin, and Afro-Atlantic communities."@en .
