<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#associatedHouse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A religious house (iroko:House) with which this society maintains an ongoing ceremonial relationship. In many traditions, society and house membership overlap for senior practitioners."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mask-function-ancestral-embodiment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The masquerade manifests an ancestral spirit or collective ancestral force. Primary function of Egungun."@en .
