<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#GovernanceStructureScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Estruturas de governança de sociedades"@pt .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#masqueradeRequiredGrade> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "required grade for performance"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#societyTradition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#TitleConferralScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#conferral-hereditary> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#gov-council-of-elders> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Governance by a council of senior members without strict linear grade hierarchy. Characteristic of Ogboni and some Egungun lineages."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#societyStatus-reformed> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The society has been reconstituted after a period of dormancy or dissolution, with continuity of tradition but a break in institutional operation."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mask-function-funerary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The masquerade participates in funerary ceremonies, guiding the deceased or honoring the passing. Abakuá íremes appear at members' funerals."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#societyType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-ekpe> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#societyType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Typological classification of the society. Range: iroko:InitiatorySocietyTypeScheme."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#gradeName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "grade name"@en .
